<title>USA: U.S. Cattle on Feed - USDA.</title>
<headline>U.S. Cattle on Feed - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-11-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>USDA U.S. cattle on feed. 7 states, 1,000-plus head feedlots (data in 1,000 head):</p>
<p>    -			Pct----1996----1995    1994</p>
<p> On Feed Nov 1	   101   8,544   8,420   7,988</p>
<p> During Oct:	     Pct----1996----1995    1994</p>
<p> -Placed on Feed	 111   2,531   2,278   2,244</p>
<p> -Marketed		  93   1,416   1,529   1,504</p>
<p> -Other Disappearance  112	57	51	47</p>
<p> On Feed Oct 1	    97   7,486   7,722   7,295</p>
<p> -			   Pct---Nov 1---Oct 1</p>
<p>  U.S. On Feed	   114  10,070   8,841</p>
<p>Analysts on average had expected the number of cattle on feed in the seven key states as of November 1 at 99.5 percent of a year ago, and October placements at 105.7 percent of a year ago.</p>
<p>The seven major states are Arizona, California, Colorado, Iowa, Kansas, Nebraska and Texas.</p>
